# Copy to `.env.development.local` (or `.env.local`) to run `npm run dev` against a real chain —
# `.env*` is gitignored repo-wide except this template, same convention as the root `.env.example`.
# Vite never loads `.env.example` itself; `vite build` (production mode) loads neither file, which
# is why a production build with nothing configured renders "not configured" rather than this data.
#
# UNLIKE THE ROOT `.env.example`, NOTHING BELOW IS A PLACEHOLDER. A public mainnet RPC and a real,
# already-deployed vault address — there is nothing secret to fill in.
#
# ARC MAINNET, LIVE AS OF 2026-09-24 (firstVault.createdAt,
# contracts/config/deployments/arc-mainnet.json — chain UTC, not a session's local date). RWAlly's
# v1 vault is deployed on Arc mainnet (chain 5042):
# the cirBTC Vault at the address below, creator Safe 0x99e805294F1f1465C96f68e36264E99991Ef9E82,
# basket cirBTC alone. `VaultFactory` 0x692385262c05df7515560886f167c4edd0814025, `Governance`
# 0x79279fba3b6f6736f07cbbfcb7cf0559466d5bfb, oracle 0x0C60b9a4C207dd622CcC0Ee3C51b5c274cb7B979 —
# all four re-read on-chain (`eth_getCode`) directly against https://rpc.mainnet.arc.io in this
# change, not copied from a prior draft. AS READ 2026-09-23 THE VAULT IS EMPTY (no deposits yet):
# a member reading this build then saw real zeros from a real chain read, not a bundled sample and
# not a fixture — read `NAV`/`holderCount` live rather than trusting this comment for the current
# figure, since a deposit makes it stale the moment it lands. Anything the RWAlly team seeds on it
# going forward is the team's own activity and must be labelled as such wherever it is shown, never
# presented as an organic member.
#
# Before this file pointed here it pointed at Base Sepolia's smoke-test fixture
# (`contracts/config/deployments/base-sepolia.json`), the one live-read path this repository could
# prove before Arc carried a deployment. That config still exists for local dev against a fixture
# vault — see `test/lib/ui-smoke-chain.mjs`, which forks Base Sepolia for the UI smoke harness —
# but it is no longer what a production build of this app reads by default.
#
# `test/csp.test.mjs`'s "connect-src names the SAME origin VITE_RPC_URL actually resolves to..."
# test reads VITE_RPC_URL out of THIS file (the one guaranteed to be committed) and asserts it
# appears in public/_headers' connect-src — change one, change the other, in the same commit.
#
# VITE_VAULT_NAME IS SET, OWNER DECISION #353. The address below is genuinely the v1 mainnet vault
# (card #67, `Decisions/Vault name is cirBTC Vault 2026-09-19`), so "cirBTC Vault" is no longer a
# false claim about a testnet fixture the way it would have been before the cutover —
# `test/vault-name.test.mjs` now asserts this file DOES set it, the inverse of what it asserted
# pre-cutover. `test/csp.test.mjs` asserts both this address and this name reach a build made the
# way Cloudflare Pages makes one (`VITE_*` as real process env vars ahead of `vite build`, not read
# from this file, which Vite never loads for a production build) — it builds its OWN bundle into a
# throwaway OS temp directory to check that, rather than the shared `dist/` this app's other tests
# use, or anywhere under this repo a concurrent `.html`-scanning test could observe mid-write.

VITE_RPC_URL=https://rpc.mainnet.arc.io
VITE_CHAIN_ID=5042
VITE_VAULT_ADDRESSES=0x4EAE5C6D753AAC0b4825d41c12e71f0a8bE579f6
VITE_VAULT_NAME=cirBTC Vault
